message.content:
You are the implementer subagent for **Task A1 + A2** of the multi-vehicle concurrency plan.

Repo: /home/ubuntu/个人学习/amr_dispatcher, branch `main` (create/switch to branch `feat/multi-vehicle-concurrency` from main).
Plan: /home/ubuntu/.claude/plans/fizzy-sparking-ripple.md (Task A section — read A1/A2/A5 and the P0 现状 table)

## Context
The project is an AMR multi-robot dispatcher. Today `dispatcher_node.cpp:2298` binds a mission to a VDA 5050 vehicle by round-robin (`vda5050_rr_cursor_ % vda5050_vehicle_ids_.size()`). We are building an explicit vehicle-assignment layer. Task A1 is a **pure core function** (zero ROS, zero MQTT); Task A2 is a **schema + plumbing** change. A3 (per-vehicle topics) and A4 (slot split) are NOT your scope — another implementer does them after you.

## A1: Core pure function `PlanVehicleAssignment`

Create:
- `src/amr_dispatcher_core/include/amr_dispatcher_core/fleet/vehicle_assignment.hpp`
- `src/amr_dispatcher_core/src/fleet/vehicle_assignment.cpp`
- `test/unit/test_vda5050_vehicle_assignment.cpp` (name it `test_vehicle_assignment` if you prefer; register in CMake accordingly)

Namespace `amr_dispatcher_core::fleet`.

Design (you may refine names, keep the semantics):
```cpp
// 单台受管车的运行时状态（轻量输入，不与 fleet.yaml 强耦合）
struct VehicleRuntimeState {
  std::string vehicle_id;
  bool online = true;      // 链路在线（VDA 5050 online 态）
  bool busy = false;       // 已被在途任务占用
  bool enabled = true;     // 运营开关
  double battery_percent = 100.0;
  std::string current_station_id;  // 已知则用于距离估算，可空
  std::vector<std::string> capabilities;  // 如 {"transport","charging"}
};

struct VehicleAssignmentRequest {
  std::string requested_vehicle_id;   // 可空：显式指定
  std::vector<VehicleRuntimeState> vehicles;
  std::string pickup_station_id;
  std::string dropoff_station_id;
  std::string required_capability = "transport";
  double min_battery_percent = 0.0;
  // 到 pickup 的直线距离（vehicle_id -> 米）；不可算则该车无此项
  std::unordered_map<std::string, double> distance_to_pickup_m;
};

struct VehicleAssignmentDecision {
  bool assigned = false;
  std::string vehicle_id;
  std::string reject_reason;
  // 决策依据（审计用）
  std::string strategy;  // "explicit" | "nearest" | "first_available" | "rejected"
};

VehicleAssignmentDecision PlanVehicleAssignment(const VehicleAssignmentRequest& request);
```

Rules — **order is fixed and must be unit-testable**:
1. `requested_vehicle_id` non-empty → the vehicle MUST exist in `vehicles`, be `online && !busy && enabled`, and possess `required_capability`; otherwise **reject** (do NOT silently reassign). If valid → `strategy="explicit"`.
2. No explicit request → filter candidates: `online && !busy && enabled && has capability && battery_percent >= min_battery_percent`.
3. Among candidates, pick the one with the smallest `distance_to_pickup_m`; ties broken by input order. If a candidate has no distance entry, it is still eligible but ranked after all candidates that have a distance. If **no** candidate has a distance entry at all → pick the first eligible candidate in input order, `strategy="first_available"`.
4. No eligible candidate → reject with a reason that says WHY (e.g. "no online vehicle with capability 'transport'", "all eligible vehicles busy", "battery below threshold").
5. Empty `vehicles` → reject "no managed vehicles configured".

Also expose a small helper the ROS side will need:
```cpp
// 该车是否具备某能力（capabilities 为空视为"无限制"，便于单车最小配置）
bool VehicleHasCapability(const VehicleRuntimeState& vehicle, const std::string& capability);
```
Decide + document the semantics of an EMPTY capabilities list. My recommendation: empty == no capability restriction (a single managed vehicle with no declared capabilities must still be selectable), but make it explicit in a comment and cover it with a test.

**Pure-core rules**: only STL includes; no ROS/MQTT; no I/O.

## A2: `Mission.fleet_id` reused as vehicle id + SubmitOrder schema

- `src/amr_dispatcher_core/include/amr_dispatcher_core/dispatcher/mission_state.hpp:42` — `std::string fleet_id = "default";  // V1.2 多机预留` → change the comment to something like `// 绑定的车辆 id（空 = 由选车策略决定）` and consider changing the default from `"default"` to `""` (empty = unassigned). **Check all usages of `fleet_id` first** — grep showed it currently has ZERO usages outside its own declaration, so changing the default is safe, but verify again and report.
- `src/amr_dispatcher_interfaces/srv/SubmitOrder.srv` — **APPEND** `string vehicle_id` at the END of the request block (do NOT reorder or rename existing fields; old clients must keep working).
- `src/amr_dispatcher_interfaces/srv/EnqueueMission.srv` — same: append `string vehicle_id`.
- `src/amr_dispatcher_ros/src/dispatcher_node.cpp` `SubmitOrderCb` — write `req->vehicle_id` into `m.fleet_id` (empty string = unassigned). Also `EnqueueMissionCb` if it builds a Mission similarly.
- `src/amr_dispatcher_tools/src/rest_gateway.cpp` — the `/api/v1/orders` handler: parse optional `vehicle` query param (name it `vehicle` to match the REST style of `id`/`from`/`to`/`prio`) and forward it into the SubmitOrder request.

**Compatibility red line**: existing e2e (`./scripts/check_vda5050_e2e.sh`) must pass unchanged — the new field is optional and empty by default.

## TDD (mandatory)
1. Write the test file FIRST; build and show it fails (missing header) — record that evidence.
2. Implement; make it green.
3. `ctest --test-dir build/core` must be 612 + your new tests, 100% passing.

Suggested test cases for A1 (write your own variants as you see fit, but cover): explicit valid; explicit unknown vehicle (reject); explicit offline (reject); explicit busy (reject); explicit missing capability (reject); auto-select nearest; auto-select ties → input order; auto-select no distance info → first eligible; capability filter excludes; battery threshold excludes; busy excluded; no eligible → reject with reason; empty vehicle list → reject; explicit request wins over a nearer auto candidate.

## Build & verify
- Core: `cmake --build build/core -j$(nproc) && ctest --test-dir build/core`
- ROS/interfaces (must compile after the .srv change): `docker exec amr_dispatcher bash -c "source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash && cd /workspace && colcon build --packages-select amr_dispatcher_interfaces amr_dispatcher_ros amr_dispatcher_tools --base-paths src"` — NOTE: from `/workspace` use `--base-paths src`, otherwise package discovery fails.
- e2e: `./scripts/check_vda5050_e2e.sh` — must still be EXIT=0 with all 8 stages PASS (this is the compatibility red line). Report the actual summary lines.

## Commits
Two logical commits:
1. `feat(core): 车辆选车策略纯函数 PlanVehicleAssignment 与任务车辆绑定字段`
2. `feat(ros): 提单链路支持显式指定车辆（SubmitOrder/EnqueueMission/REST）`
Each ends with:
Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

## Report back
Files touched, commit SHAs, red-light evidence, final test counts (before/after), e2e summary lines, any deviation from this brief and why, and anything A3/A4 implementers must know (e.g. exact field names, where `m.fleet_id` is set, how ROS should build `VehicleRuntimeState` from `vda5050_links_` + `config/fleet.yaml`).

